    <section id="overview">
      <h2>Company overview</h2>
      <p>
        Zhejiang Shuntong Electric Co., Ltd., trading under the brand name SNTOOM, is a Chinese manufacturer
        specializing in electromechanical equipment. The company produces a range of industrial fans and
        motor‑driven warning sirens used in factories, civil‑defense systems, and general emergency signaling.
      </p>
      <p>
        Among its product lines, SNTOOM is particularly known for the MS‑series motorized sirens, a family of compact
        and medium‑sized sirens designed for both indoor and outdoor applications.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="products">
      <h2>Products</h2>

      <h3>Industrial fans</h3>
      <p>
        SNTOOM manufactures various industrial ventilation fans intended for workshops, warehouses, and other
        environments requiring reliable air circulation and cooling. These products typically feature robust
        housings, high‑efficiency motors, and options for wall‑mounted or portable installation.
      </p>

      <h3>MS‑series motor sirens</h3>
      <p>
        The MS‑series is a family of electromechanical motor sirens covering a range of sizes and output levels.
        Models commonly referenced include MS‑190, MS‑290, MS‑390, MS‑490, MS‑590, MS‑690, and MS‑790. They are
        used for industrial alarms, emergency warnings, and civil‑defense signaling.
      </p>

      Products *STUB*

    <section id="applications">
      <h2>Applications</h2>
      <p>
        SNTOOM sirens are typically installed in factories, chemical plants, construction sites, and public
        warning systems. Depending on the model, they can be configured for fire alarms, evacuation signals,
        machinery fault alerts, and general emergency notifications.
      </p>
    </section>
